 "source": "Espressif ESP32-DevKitC V4 getting-started guide and board dimensions: PCB 54.4 x 27.9 mm, NO mounting holes, micro-USB B receptacle on one short end, 2 x 19 pin headers with the rows 25.4 mm apart (1.0 in, 2.54 mm pitch), ESP32-WROOM-32 module (18.0 x 25.5 x 3.1 mm per its datasheet) at the other end with the PCB antenna at the board edge. ASSUMED / uncertain: PCB thickness 1.6 mm; header pins point UP (male pins soldered, plastic 2.5 mm on top, 8.5 mm pin height above the PCB, 3 mm tails below); micro-USB 7.5 x 5.9 x 2.9 mm with 1.0 mm overhang (+/-0.5) centred across the width; first-pin offset from the USB end (headers assumed centred along the length); tallest other top part 3.6 mm (EN/BOOT tact switches); antenna keep-out: module antenna zone 6.0 mm long, plus 8.0 mm of free space past the board end and 5.0 mm free above the module (brief G03 asks for 8 mm; Espressif's hardware guidelines recommend at least 15 mm of free board, no metal, and the zone beyond the module edge clear of walls).",
