 "notes": "The board has no mounting holes and no HOLE datum: the design must hold it by edge ribs, clips or a pocket. Hold it at the long edges (EDGE_LONG_A / EDGE_LONG_B planes) on strips that lie OUTSIDE the header footprint: the rows are 25.4 mm apart on a 27.9 mm board, so the clear land outside each row is only 0.25 mm wide before the pin tails (rows centre 1.25 mm from the edge, header body 2.54 wide), so a rib must grip the board edge itself from above and below, or rest on the PCB underside in the end regions ahead of / behind the pin tails (the headers span x = 4.3 to 50.1). The USB end (x < 4.3) and the module end are the clear lands for support. antenna_zone keepout: no wall or lid material above the module's antenna end and for antenna_clear_beyond past the board end (a no-material region; a lid that spans over the module must stop before x = pcb_length - antenna_zone_length or be open there). Header pins point up (tips 8.5 mm over the PCB, the dupont-wire envelope) and the pins' tails 3 mm under, keepout to avoid the lid/ribs; if the owner has the pins soldered the other way round, swap pin_height_above and pin_tail_length. Import gate: R1 PCB 54.4 x 27.9; R3 USB along -X; R4 overhang assumed (tol 0.5); R9 skipped.",
